   "": {
    "actClause": "AN ACT to amend the alcoholic beverage control law, in relation to exempting\ncertain parcels of land from licensing restrictions for manufacturers and\nwholesalers of alcoholic beverages who sell at retail for on-premises\nconsumption",
    "basePrintNo": "S8443",
    "basePrintNoStr": "S8443-2023",
    "coSponsors": {
     "items": [],
     "size": 0
    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "Amd §101, ABC L",
    "lawSection": "Alcoholic Beverage Control Law",
    "memo": " \nBILL NUMBER: S8443\n\nSPONSOR: PALUMBO\n \nTITLE OF BILL:\n\nAn act to amend the alcoholic beverage control law, in relation to\nexempting certain parcels of land from licensing restrictions for\nmanufacturers and wholesalers of alcoholic beverages who sell at retail\nfor on-premises consumption\n\n \nPURPOSE:\n\nTo amend Chapter 328 of the Laws of 2022 by providing the metes and\nbounds of the new location of Talkhouse Encore, in the town of East\nHampton.\n\n \nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\n\nSection 1. Amends subparagraph (xiv) of paragraph (a) of section 101(1)\nof the alcoholic beverage control law by replacing the metes and bounds\nof Talkhouse Encore in the town of East Hampton that is on the list of\nparcels which are exempt from the tied-house laws.\n\nSection 2. Sets forth the effective date.\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nSince the 1930's, when Prohibition was repealed, New York State law has\nrestricted holders of alcohol manufacturing/wholesale/importer licenses\nfrom having an interest in a retail license and vice versa.  Known as\nthe \"tied-house\" laws, efforts have been made to modernize the law by\naddressing these types of archaic ownership issues.\n\nIn the meantime, these provisions have been amended on occasion by\nexempting certain properties to support local economic development\ngoals. This was done, for example, through the enactment of Chapter 328\nof the Laws of 2022 which exempted the Stephen Talkhouse (the bar) and\nTalkhouse Encore (local drink brand), as described by the metes and\nbounds of each parcel, located in the town of East Hampton.  Since then,\nthe offices of Talkhouse Encore as moved. Therefore, this legislation is\nnecessary to amend Chapter 328 by replacing the metes and bounds of the\nold location with the coordinates of the new parcel, so it is accurately\nreflected in the alcoholic beverage control law.\n\n \nLEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\nNew bill\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS:\n\nThis legislation will help generate sales, excise and property tax\nrevenue\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nImmediately\n",
